  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Integrated Resilience Programme (MIRP) for North West Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The MIRP project in North West Nigeria aims to bolster community resilience and prevent malnutrition in vulnerable populations. Recognizing the complex interplay of factors contributing to malnutrition, the project integrates interventions across health, agriculture, water, sanitation, and hygiene (WASH), and social protection sectors. Key activities include promoting climate-smart agricultural practices to enhance diverse food production especially amongst child caregivers, improving access to essential health and nutrition services, particularly for women and young children, and establishing community-based management of acute malnutrition. Furthermore, the project will strengthen local food systems, empower communities with nutrition knowledge and hygiene practices, and advocate for policies that support sustainable nutritional well-being. By addressing both immediate and underlying causes of malnutrition, this initiative seeks to build long-term resilience against food insecurity and economic shocks prevalent in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
